WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.680
- Well, the job you're best
known for, obviously, is SNL.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.808
So what do you miss about the show?

00:00:04.808 --> 00:00:06.900
- I miss so much about it.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.020
I miss the people.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:12.440
I truly miss the immediacy
of coming up with a joke

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:16.050
on Monday, spending 20 hours not sleeping

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:19.300
with friends who haven't slept either

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.570
and making up dumb jokes,

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.480
and then putting it on television
at the end of the week.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.030
And having everybody see
it, that, I miss that.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.660
I miss the immediacy of,
like, ooh, I got this idea.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.493
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:29.326
- And then it being.

00:00:29.326 --> 00:00:30.310
- [Kelly] Then it comes
to fruition very quickly.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.360
- On live television on the show

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.410
you always wished you were on.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.340
- Yeah, at the same time though,

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.100
'cause I've known a couple of
people that have hosted that,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.120
and the hours that y'all keep are insane.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:41.967
- Yeah, truly insane.

00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:44.270
- Like, I don't like, do you sleep?

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.580
- Then, no.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:46.720
I mean, well, it depends.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:47.740
Some weeks, yes.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.860
Some weeks, you're depressed and sleeping

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:50.760
'cause you're not in the show.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.140
And then some weeks, and then some weeks,

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.290
you can't think because
you're in everything,

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.770
and then some weeks, same thing,

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:59.475
but then the second the show
starts, it all gets cut, and -

00:00:59.475 --> 00:01:00.460
- [Kelly] That happens?

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.293
- Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:02.126
- Yes.

00:01:02.126 --> 00:01:02.959
- That sounds stressful.

00:01:02.959 --> 00:01:03.792
- It was very stressful.

00:01:03.792 --> 00:01:04.625
- I know, I always thought,

00:01:04.625 --> 00:01:05.530
because I've performed on it,

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.760
and I always thought, oh my gosh.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.010
So what happened to like
three or four of those skits?

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:09.843
They're just like gone.

00:01:09.843 --> 00:01:11.720
And I'm like, well,
all that work is like -

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.590
- My first show, I
remember they did, like,

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.610
a Justice League sketch with Mike.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.560
It was Michael Phelps was
the host, and he was Aquaman.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.850
And the whole joke was
they were telling him

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.450
that they were firing
him because they didn't,

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:22.359
he didn't really do much.

00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:26.097
And it was a really funny sketch, but,

00:01:26.097 --> 00:01:27.000
and it was this beautiful thing.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.660
Everyone full costume, superheroes,

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.720
they built the Hall of Justice,

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:30.553
and they're like, that's cut.

00:01:30.553 --> 00:01:33.508
And I'm like, that's a
house. That cost a house.

00:01:33.508 --> 00:01:34.740
- Now, I know, and I'm going to tell you,

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.140
there is, I wish I remembered the skit,

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.510
but there was this one thing I saw

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:39.343
when I was performing there,

00:01:39.343 --> 00:01:40.610
And I was like, that was my,

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:42.280
one of my favorite things that happened

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.680
'cause I was there the whole day.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.950
I could see the whole
show and the rehearsal.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.410
And I was like, why, who got rid of that?

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.770
I was so mad about it,
and I'm not even involved.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:51.680
But I was like, that was so funny.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.960
- I can't believe you've never hosted.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:53.793
You're hilarious.

00:01:53.793 --> 00:01:54.717
- No.

00:01:54.717 --> 00:01:55.550
- People are like, you should host.

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:56.800
- Oh, I can't believe I host a show.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:57.730
I never, oh, no,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.984
I literally, I used to say no to, like,

00:01:59.984 --> 00:02:02.050
saying, "And the award goes to."

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.010
Like, I would be terrified
to read a teleprompter,

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:04.953
cut to now.

